    "created_at": "2026-06-24T12:24:43Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-06-24T12:24:43Z",
    "body": "I had not realized that the typed OM uses different objects for each of the different syntaxes. That seems rather annoying. For this particular control we should be able to always return a https://drafts.css-houdini.org/css-typed-om/#csscolor I'd think. (When the control serializes we only ever end up with hexadecimal due to legacy requirements, otherwise we always go with `color()`. There's no legacy requirements for a new object endpoint.)",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
